    "result_text": "All 3 acceptance tests pass and the build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nI agree with the finding \u2014 the city\u2192region table was duplicated byte-for-byte between `OwnerMapper` and `ClinicServiceImpl`, creating exactly the silent-divergence risk the review describes. I hoisted it to a single source of truth:\n\n- **New `model/Region.java`** \u2014 holds the one city\u2192region `Map` and exposes `forCity(city)` (returns `null` for unknown, the shape the validator wants) and `localityForCity(city)` (returns `\"UNKNOWN\"`, the shape the presentation layer wants).\n- **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 removed its `CITY_REGION` constant; `addLocality` now calls `Region.localityForCity(...)`. Also dropped the now-unused `java.util.Map` import.\n- **`ClinicServiceImpl`** \u2014 removed its `CITY_REGION` constant; `assertPostcodeValid` now calls `Region.forCity(...)`. The `REGION_POSTCODES` range table stays in the service, since it's validation-specific \u2014 matching the reviewer's own guidance.\n\nBoth layers now read the mapping from `Region`, so a city or region change happens in exactly one place. Acceptance behaviour is unchanged and the suite is green.",
